* FD-29  Operating supply range, DC sweep (spec 3.3.2.1) for the FD-01
* application: inputs and vcm at VDD/2, VDD swept 0 .. {{VDD_MAX}} V in 10 mV steps,
* bias current scaled with VDD.  A {{V_PROBE}} V differential input is applied so a
* dead amplifier cannot pass: it works while Vod tracks the input and the
* output common mode tracks VDD/2, each within 10 mV of its value at nominal VDD.
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-6 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-9
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
EVCM vcm 0 vdd 0 {{VCM_FRACTION}}
BIBIAS vdd ibias I = {{IBIAS}} * min(1, max(0, v(vdd)) / {{VDD}})
VIP vip vcm {{V_PROBE_HALF}}
VIN vin vcm {{V_PROBE_HALF_NEG}}
R1 vip inp {{R_NET}}
R2 inp outn {{R_NET}}
R3 vin inn {{R_NET}}
R4 inn outp {{R_NET}}
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn vcm {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
dc vdd 0 {{VDD_MAX}} 0.01
write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn) v(vcm)
.endc
.end
